# Test: with no daemon, validate starts no external plugin and says its section is not available
#
# Question: when `ze config validate` runs with no daemon on a config that
# declares an external plugin and holds a section under that plugin's root,
# does it refuse the section with the reason and the command that reaches a
# running ze, without starting the program the config names? And does it still
# accept a config that holds no such section, and a compiled-in plugin?
# Why not a unit test: TestValidateRefusesSectionOfExternalPluginWithoutStartingIt
# proves the validate function. This proves the `ze` binary an operator runs:
# no route from the command line to a fork of the declared program, and the
# message as it is printed.
#
# The declared program writes a marker file when it is started, in any mode,
# and then answers a declaration query the way a conforming plugin does. Under
# the behaviour the owner ruled out, validate ran it in declare mode, the
# marker appeared and the section was accepted. Step 4 starts the same program
# by hand: its marker is the control that the script writes one where the test
# looks.
#
# Source of the contract (Thomas): "plugin command requiring external plugins
# which can not be started from the code when no daemon is running to pass it
# to are not available, for command built-in then yes you should run them as
# we can look them up in the yang hardcoded in the binary".
#
# VALIDATES: AC-2 and AC-15 of spec-plugin-external-yang-at-startup, as the
#   ruling restates them.
# PREVENTS: inspecting a config someone else wrote running their command; a
#   bare "unknown top-level keyword" with no word about why; validate refusing
#   every config that declares an external plugin.

tmpfs=marker.run:mode=755:terminator=EOF_RUN
#!/bin/sh
# Leaves a marker named after its first argument, then answers a declaration
# query; refuses a live start.
echo started > "started-$1.marker"
if [ "$ZE_PLUGIN_MODE" != "declare" ]; then
	exit 1
fi
cat <<'EOF_DECLARATION'
#1 ze-plugin-engine:declare-registration {"protocol-version":1,"wants-config":["acme-shell"],"schema":{"module":"acme-shell-conf","namespace":"urn:acme:shell:conf","yang-text":"module acme-shell-conf { namespace \"urn:acme:shell:conf\"; prefix shell; container acme-shell { presence \"The acme shell plugin is configured\"; leaf greeting { type string { length \"1..64\"; } } } }"}}
EOF_DECLARATION
EOF_RUN

tmpfs=ze.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external acme-shell {
		run "./marker.run by-ze"
		encoder json
	}
}

acme-shell {
	greeting hello
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=no-section.conf:terminator=EOF_NO_SECTION
plugin {
	external acme-shell {
		run "./marker.run by-ze"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_NO_SECTION

tmpfs=built-in.conf:terminator=EOF_BUILT_IN
plugin {
	internal static {
		use static
	}
}
EOF_BUILT_IN

# The section of the external plugin is refused, with why and the command that
# reaches a running ze.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate ze.conf:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=unknown top-level keyword: acme-shell
expect=stdout:contains=the config declares external plugin "acme-shell"
expect=stdout:contains=starts no plugin
expect=stdout:contains=show config validation ze.conf
expect=stdout:contains=fix: ze cli

# A config that declares the plugin and holds no section of it is valid.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate no-section.conf:exit=0
reject=stdout:contains=external plugin "acme-shell"
reject=stdout:contains=unknown top-level keyword

# A compiled-in plugin is judged with the schema in the binary, as before.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze config validate built-in.conf:exit=0

# Control: started by hand, the program leaves its marker in this directory.
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=sh marker.run by-test:exit=1

expect=file:path=started-by-test.marker:exists=true
expect=file:path=started-by-ze.marker:absent=true
